or   $A[An + B] + B = [An + B + n]/2 - K$ ;

or  $A^2n + AB + B = [(A+1)/2]n + (B/2 - K)$  (iii).

Matching up the coefficients of like-terms now produces: $A^2 = (A+1)/2  \Rightarrow 2A^2 - A - 1 = (2A+1)(A-1) = 0 \Rightarrow A = 1, -1/2$  (of which only  $A = 1$  is admissible for  $f(n)))$ . $AB + B = B/2 - K  \Rightarrow  2B = B/2 - K  \Rightarrow  -3B/2 = K$ .

